{{Quote|You know how particular the Roonan are.|[[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]]|<ref name="Evil Plans" />}}
The '''Roonan''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that were [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Roona]]. The Roonan had [[Color|blue]] or gray skin and they had a ridged forehead and cranium with large, almond-shaped blue [[eye]]s. Short in stature, they had big ideas and were notoriously easy to offend. They were known to take even the slightest slip-up as a deep insult. The [[Jedi Master]] [[Halsey]] was a member of this species, as were Senators [[Aang]] and [[Edcel Bar Gane]]. According to [[C-3PO]], the Roonan had tiny [[Tooth|teeth]]. They were reputed for being very picky and particular regarding details; the slightest error could be taken as a grievous insult.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Clone-wars-roonan-ears.png|thumb|left|200px|The ears of a Roonan.]]
Roonans were a bipedal species, possessing two [[Limb|arms]] and two legs. Their arms ended in hands similar in structure to those of [[Neimoidian]]s. Their bodies were fairly humanoid in proportions. They had ridged heads with grooves extending along the cranium to the back of their head, one of which formed the structure of their ears. Their skin was blue-gray, and they had large, almond-shaped, bulging eyes. Their heads were completely hairless, and they lacked a visible [[nose]]. <ref name="Alien Archive" />
==History==
Roonans hailed from Roona,<ref name="Alien Archive" /> an astronomical object in the [[Bes Ber Bikade sector]] of the [[Expansion Region]]<ref name="Appendix">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}}</ref> An entry on Roonans, featuring an image of a Roonan in blue [[clothing]], was included in an [[Unidentified artist|artist]]’s [[Unidentified artist's journal|journal]], which was later restored, expanded, and displayed at the [[Graf Archive]]. It also noted that Roonans, while known to have big ideas, were known to be notoriously easy to defend. The entry also noted that Roonans possessed tiny teeth, although it cautioned that directly questioning a Roonan might be unwise.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> This entry appeared at some point no earlier than [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Year">{{AlienArchiveJournalDate}}</ref>

==Roonan in the Galaxy==
During the High Republic era in [[382 BBY]],<ref name="CatDate">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]'' dates the events of ''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]'', including the [[death]] of Goi Ganok on [[Eirie]], to [[382 BBY]].</ref> [[Goi Ganok]] was a Roonan [[Gender|male]] member of the [[Path of the Open Hand]]. He and [[Binnot Ullo]] were dispatched by [[Elecia Zeveron|the Mother]] to carry out a mission intended to reignite the [[Eiram and E'ronoh War|war]] between [[Eiram]] and [[E'ronoh]]. Though he eventually [[death|killed]] himself by detonating a canister he was holding.<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref> In [[230 BBY]],<ref name="230BBYDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''The High Republic: The Battle for Starlight'' to [[230 BBY]].</ref> a Roonan resident of [[Eiram]] tried to flee the world due to the groundquakes and storms on the planet. Jedi arrived to help the fleeing citizens including the Roonan.<ref name="Battle for Starlight">''[[The High Republic: The Battle for Starlight]]''</ref> During the late Republic Era, in [[23 BBY]],<ref name="23BBYDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''Age of Republic - Jango Fett'' 1 to [[23 BBY]].</ref> two Roonan bartenders operated within a cantina on [[Ord Mantell]] when [[Jango Fett]] and a band of [[Bounty hunter|bounty hunters]] tracked down a [[Twi'lek]] woman who was meeting with a [[Falleen]] named [[Griph]].<ref name="Age of Republic Jango">[[Age of Republic - Jango Fett 1|''Age of Republic - Jango Fett'' 1]]</ref>

[[File:Seles-ReturnToVadersCastle1.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Seles, a roonan youngling who as dropped off on Lotho Minor]]
During the [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul|Darth Maul]]'s imprisonment on [[Lotho Minor]], the droid [[pirate]] Captain [[Spikewheel]] dropped off younglings of various species, including the Roonan [[Seles]], in an effort to test whether they were worthy to join his crew. As part of this trial, Spikewheel required that the younglings survive one night on Lotho Minro, believing that their survival would indicate potential for service in his operations.<ref name="RTVC 1">[[Star Wars Adventures: Return to Vader's Castle 1|''Star Wars Adventures: Return to Vader's Castle'' 1]]</ref> 

The Roonan Halsey was a [[Gender|male]] [[Jedi Master]] who served during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Monster">{{TCW|Monster}}</ref> In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Intrigue Date">{{TCWcanondates|209}}</ref> Halsey was present in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] war room, observing a [[hologram]] depicting [[Jedi]] Master [[Eeth Koth]] being tortured by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[General]] [[Grievous]].<ref name="Grievous Intrigue old EP guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode209.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Grievous Intrigue}}</ref> In [[20 BBY]],<ref name="Date1">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of "[[Monster]]," which include the [[Devaron]] massacre and death of Halsey, to [[20 BBY]].</ref> Halsey and his [[Padawan]] [[Knox]] were sent to the [[Temple of Eedit]] on the [[planet]] [[Devaron]] to [[Devaron massacre|defend]] it from the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]’ [[Separatist Droid Army|Droid Army]]. During the battle, [[Count]] [[Dooku]]’s new [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]], [[Savage Opress]], arrived, slaughtering the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[clone trooper]]s defending the temple. With only Halsey and his [[Padawan]] [[Knox]] left, Halsey ordered his Padawan to stay back and engaged Opress directly. During the duel, Opress seized Halsey’s hand, causing him to drop [[Halsey's lightsaber|his lightsaber]]. In the ensuing melee, Halsey was overpowered and ultimately struck down when Opress impaled him with [[Savage's spear|his]] [[spear]]. Attempting to avenge his master, Knox charged at Opress, only to be thrown against the temple gates and killed on impact.<ref name="Monster">{{TCW|Monster}}</ref>

[[File:EdcelBarGaneSenate-POP.png|thumb|left|230px|Senator Edcel Bar Gane speaks with his aide]]
Also during the Clone Wars, the Roonan senator [[Aang]] represented the planet Roona.<ref name="TBoCW">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Clone Wars Begin}}</ref> During the war, he served on the [[Military Oversight Committee]] and was persuaded by the Naboo senator [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] to vote in favor of reducing [[Republic military enhancement bill|funding]] for the Grand Army of the Republic.<ref name="Evil Plans">{{TCW|Evil Plans}}</ref> Despite Aang’s support, the Senate ultimately approved an increase in military spending to provide the army with five million additional clone troopers.<ref name="SM">{{TCW|Senate Murders}}</ref> Following the [[Alderaan Refugee Conference|Conference on Alderaan]], Senator Amidala hosted a party in his honor.<ref name="Evil Plans">{{TCW|Evil Plans}}</ref> The Roonan senator [[Edcel Bar Gane]] also served during the Clone Wars. He was known for his striking ice-blue eyes.<ref name="Geektionary">[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]</ref> He was accompanied by a Roonan aide during Padme Amidala's opposition speech to the senate on a bill to increase funding of the war.<ref name="Pursuit">{{TCW|Pursuit of Peace}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Roonans were first developed for [[George Lucas]]'s [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace]]. But were not seen in the film itself.<ref name="SWCTP">''[[Star Wars Chronicles: The Prequels]]''</ref>

